 "level_notes": {
  "1": "The Power ISA book (OpenPOWER Foundation, free with click-through license) is normative; the ELFv1/ELFv2 ABIs define calling conventions. The POWER memory model was formalised by the Cambridge/INRIA herd work.",
  "0": "No reference implementation; GNU as, LLVM, IBM's AIX assembler and QEMU are the main implementations."
